# API reference documentation (`docs/api/`)

Enable only when the **`api-docs`** module was selected at `cursor init` (or `render.sh --modules api-docs`).

## Purpose

Close gaps where **OpenAPI alone** is insufficient: query allowlists, pagination envelopes, auth scopes, error codes, lifecycle semantics, and frontend-oriented view → API mapping.

## Authoring contract

Read and follow **[docs/api/AGENTS.md](../../docs/api/AGENTS.md)** for chapter outline, quality bar, and subagent delegation rules.

| Doc | Role |
|-----|------|
| [docs/api/README.md](../../docs/api/README.md) | Route map, precedence, maintainer checklist |
| [docs/api/conventions.md](../../docs/api/conventions.md) | Cross-cutting prefix, auth, money/time, errors |
| [docs/api/pagination-sorting-and-query-keys.md](../../docs/api/pagination-sorting-and-query-keys.md) | List contracts master table |
| Domain `docs/api/<domain>.md` | Per-area depth (mirror reference chapter in AGENTS.md) |

## When to delegate

For **new domain chapters** or **many routes in one pass**, spawn a documentation subagent with disjoint ownership (`docs/api/**` only)—see **Subagent orchestration** in AGENTS.md. Parent keeps handler/tests work separate.

## Stack paths (customize in AGENTS.md / conventions)

- Routes: `backend/<route-registry>`
- Handlers: `backend/<handlers>/`
- Schemas: `backend/<schemas>/`
- OpenAPI: `backend/openapi/openapi.yaml`

See [docs/stack-api-reference.md](../../docs/stack-api-reference.md).
